Add a Codex palette that makes the web UI look like the Codex desktop app.

Codex sits next to the other palettes in Settings -> Appearance and works in
light and dark mode. themePalette.ts adds its colour tokens (neutral greys,
black or white primary, a blue accent) and themePalettes.generated.css is
regenerated from them. codexTheme.css changes the layout under
[data-theme="codex"]: the native system font, a flat grey sidebar with
compact rows, user messages in a borderless grey bubble, "Worked" folds
followed by a hairline, flat code blocks without line numbers, a rounder
composer with a round send button and the workspace bar beneath it, its
labels on one baseline whatever the fonts, a terminal mark instead of the
mascot on the new-session screen, and rounder menus. The other palettes
are unchanged. Applies after 0010-fast-mode-command-lifecycle.patch.
Base: omnigent v0.15.0 (c8b9b85f822f).

